          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "1. 5125                          STUDHAM                           CHURCH END Church of St Mary TL 01 NW 42/288                    3.2.67 I 2. Flint rubble and Totternhoe stone, cement rendered.  Fine early C13 arcades of 4 bays with 3 types of capitals; scalloped, foliated and moulded.  Chancel, aisles, clerestorey and west tower are Perpendicular and plain.  Repairs were carried out early C19 when the vestry was added.  C13 font with band of leaves and dragons around upper part.  Chancel window has Kempe glass of 1903. Listing NGR: TL0159115976"
    }
